; An AXTAG key one slip from a key the compiler checks.
;
; The key namespace is OPEN by decision - `checkOneAxtag` records that
; the key is "metadata stage0 records and does not check" - and this
; does not close it. `agent:readonly` and `totallyMadeUpKey` below draw
; nothing, and must not: a key carrying `:` is namespaced and
; deliberate by construction, and a genuinely novel key is metadata.
;
; What is reported is the shape that COSTS something. `;@axiom:efect(pure)`
; is not a purity claim, so nothing checks it as one: `slipped` performs
; IO under a tag that reads like a guarantee and drew no AX3010 at all.
; The tag bought silence, which is worse than writing no tag, because a
; reader spends trust on it.
;
; `RESTRICT` is a slip through case, and `effct` is a second slip of
; `effect`. `effect(pure)` itself is silent, which is the control. A
; slip of `pure` is AX3078, an error (1031).
;@axiom:efect(pure)
(:: slipped (-> Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (slipped n)
  (__syscall3 1 1 n 0))

;@axiom:RESTRICT(no-io)
(:: shouted (-> Int Int))
(fn (shouted n)
  n)

;@axiom:effct(io)
(:: other (-> Int Int))
(fn (other n)
  n)

;@axiom:agent:readonly
(:: namespaced (-> Int Int))
(fn (namespaced n)
  n)

;@axiom:totallyMadeUpKey(x)
(:: novel (-> Int Int))
(fn (novel n)
  n)

;@axiom:effect(pure)
(:: control (-> Int Int))
(fn (control n)
  n)

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  0)
